2277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-39623/selection/ma-v1/821035d2ac93710d8da6b231bbd71e140c7979495c47590c1845a67ef2976ae3/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-39623/selection/ma-v1/821035d2ac93710d8da6b231bbd71e140c7979495c47590c1845a67ef2976ae3/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-39623/selection/ma-v1/821035d2ac93710d8da6b231bbd71e140c7979495c47590c1845a67ef2976ae3/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-39623/selection/ma-v1/821035d2ac93710d8da6b231bbd71e140c7979495c47590c1845a67ef2976ae3/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-39623/selection/ma-v1/821035d2ac93710d8da6b231bbd71e140c7979495c47590c1845a67ef2976ae3/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39623"] :question/problem "For the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $H={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $V={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}},{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-2)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1)=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is orthogonal to the set $H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =1\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-1)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{3} & =1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot (-1)=-2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is *not* orthogonal to the set $V.$\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =1\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 4+1\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =1\\cdot (2)+1\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1=2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is *not* orthogonal to the set $W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39623/selection/ma-v1/821035d2ac93710d8da6b231bbd71e140c7979495c47590c1845a67ef2976ae3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80501/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "91416fb9-c106-57d3-bc8e-6b7031924fd8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80501/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c462ddfc-dacc-5a0f-b219-a9d23b987ae0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80501/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d46cfe09-6563-588d-b549-8ca5cc9a7673" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80501/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c73d1929-a25f-50f3-a3c0-4b1573519a38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80501/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "4d81c3d3-21c9-5426-a430-3b4ee2454892" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80501/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f10d5a3-1e06-58d3-b2de-b7ecad475aaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80501/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-80501/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-80501/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-80501/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-80501/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80501/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80501" :question/id #uuid "b4e9d2c3-0185-539c-af7c-b2fafdc3f5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-80501" :question/problem "For the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $u⊥H,\\,$ where $H={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u⊥V,\\,$ where $V={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u⊥W,\\,$ where $W={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}},{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 2=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =2\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 1=-5\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 1=2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸V.$ Notice that we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =2\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80501/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b03ea89-5152-5ff4-813a-ca985d60ed5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80501"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39630"] :question/problem "For the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $u⊥H,\\,$ where $H={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u⊥V,\\,$ where $V={[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u⊥W,\\,$ where $W={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}},{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 3=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)=-3\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸V.$ Notice that we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 8=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80500/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6b1926d7-a020-5cbc-be3c-cf1c86cca801" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80500/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "ea0a9a47-2dd0-5339-ae25-9816af2363db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80500/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "01575bd0-ec74-5d36-bf32-d99ac07c2904" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80500/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ed82545d-2a4f-537a-8095-616f56c8565a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80500/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "0936b5e9-a41a-5dc1-ad92-f7a55ee2bf69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80500/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74b3bdf6-4a8f-50ce-8a92-4a38c8247624" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80500/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-80500/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80500/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-80500/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-80500/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-80500/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80500" :question/id #uuid "43395a07-7c5c-5ed1-938a-d890d23531a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-80500" :question/problem "For the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $H={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $V={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}},{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0=-2 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is not orthogonal to the set $H.$ Notice that we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot (-1)=1\\ne 0 &  & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, $u$ is not orthogonal to the set $H.$ Notice that, again,  we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-1)=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80500/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b03ea89-5152-5ff4-813a-ca985d60ed5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80500"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80504/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "6ccbdbc7-e03c-52f2-b162-09b518d95a38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80504/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ce942a27-1399-5d7e-b428-585e564789dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80504/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "334e5ee6-f86b-5758-bf87-93c56cb4334f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80504/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "87f51194-9db1-50e9-bbc9-39044a43f290" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80504/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "640ebf3c-6637-507d-857d-d581fc94bdb3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80504/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "abe3cf4d-40aa-5c2b-9b5a-1911f9a3e716" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80504/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-80504/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-80504/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-80504/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-80504/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-80504/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80504" :question/id #uuid "8fcfdcaf-2d9f-5535-a1fc-a07761b92dec" :question/math-academy-id "q-80504" :question/problem "For the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $V={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $H={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $V,H$- and $W$ as ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}},{{h}_{1},{h}_{2}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =3\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)=0\\,✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =3\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3=5\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is not orthogonal to the set $V.$ Notice that we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\n- For the set $H:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =3\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-2)=0,\\,✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =3\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1=0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is orthogonal to the set $H.$\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 4=4\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u$ is not orthogonal to the set $W.$ Notice that we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80504/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b03ea89-5152-5ff4-813a-ca985d60ed5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80504"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80535/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "8211f2a2-1254-5244-91c5-7e54eab3716f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80535/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "c83fe86e-bcf8-5333-aba0-15d8f645e4cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80535/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "a603744a-7b57-5993-a204-c242a3fbbb0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80535/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "1f793c13-3638-5f12-b386-01fafec9e4dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80535/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "88547203-5295-5962-ab6d-607592d7cfbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80535/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1bde0ca-be00-595a-a128-fbe6fe79d17d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80535/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-80535/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-80535/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-80535/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-80535/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-80535/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80535" :question/id #uuid "996c67e0-4eb8-54bd-95e8-5e926007963e" :question/math-academy-id "q-80535" :question/problem "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero  vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{c}{a+b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=2,$ we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=-5,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=2.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{c}{a+b}=\\frac{2}{-5+(-1)}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80535/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9aa43961-5b6a-5c8b-adea-809d0a693cd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80535"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80538/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "8470d6c4-ca04-5f3d-a129-08ffe79874f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80538/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "9742de96-45eb-5ed3-b079-484fe0609ee3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80538/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "043fb885-5c82-5d19-92cd-07c5efbb2f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80538/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "3541c31c-791e-5cc1-8ac8-f3b3a7128207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80538/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f2adab80-4b2f-5869-a6eb-541ee8300a32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80538/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d231cfbe-b195-5918-8b28-5eb5aa88cc19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80538/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-80538/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-80538/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-80538/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-80538/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-80538/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80538" :question/id #uuid "b2f638a3-52dd-5aeb-8f41-e7b02ea6bb20" :question/math-academy-id "q-80538" :question/problem "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{b}{a+c}.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=4$, we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=-10,$ $b=-3,$ and $c=4.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{b}{a+c}=\\frac{-3}{-10+4}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80538/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9aa43961-5b6a-5c8b-adea-809d0a693cd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80538"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-71102"] :question/problem "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero  vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{c}{a+b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=2,$ we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=1,$ $b=1,$ and $c=2.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{c}{a+b}=\\frac{2}{1+1}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80537/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "1f569f2a-0a1a-55de-9794-f9dd192504e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80537/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "4d150da8-c504-564b-8b2f-ad3dab9bb511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80537/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "0f22b530-cacf-56f1-8e89-1eda726833be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80537/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "c0994f64-b0f6-5baf-a085-5d9807301433" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80537/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "fe6e6318-40a7-5104-89ce-0af44ae24cf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80537/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e967f6-2fd9-5176-9965-3863c275266f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80537/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-80537/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-80537/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-80537/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-80537/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-80537/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80537" :question/id #uuid "4da05a37-ec63-5545-abce-ccdafebfd7db" :question/math-academy-id "q-80537" :question/problem "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{a+b}{c}.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=1$, we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=1.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a+b}{c}=\\frac{1+(-2)}{1}=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80537/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9aa43961-5b6a-5c8b-adea-809d0a693cd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80532/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "3d9d52fd-ebef-5612-942a-a962b5ad6420" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80532/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "af29897a-31e1-5f99-af24-cb6c66a29c58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80532/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "b2c5f930-c6b2-524f-a358-d2648cf36ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80532/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b5e4a51f-4e25-5105-8e30-2df87efc371d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80532/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "f2fa4fe6-5c66-58c1-8f24-cc05c05dd476" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80532/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad77c456-60b3-5ec0-ab5c-f052fc9fd602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80532/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-80532/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-80532/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-80532/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-80532/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-80532/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80532" :question/id #uuid "9b90f9f7-06ed-50e2-83d2-b6c61501a094" :question/math-academy-id "q-80532" :question/problem "Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]$ is a non-zero  vector that is orthogonal to the set $W={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]},$ find the value of $\\frac{a+c}{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The vector $u$ is orthogonal to the set $W$ if $u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0$ and $u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-10{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=3,$ we get the vector \n$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we obtain $a=5,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a+c}{b}=\\frac{5+3}{4}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80532/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9aa43961-5b6a-5c8b-adea-809d0a693cd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80532"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39631"] :question/problem "Consider the vector subspace $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}.$ Which of the following vectors belong to ${H}^{⊥}?$\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}$ and ${h}_{2}.$ \n\nNow, a vector $v$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $v$ is orthogonal to the set of vectors that spans the subspace $H.$ So, we have to find the products ${v}_{i}\\cdot {h}_{j}$ for $i=1,2,3$ and  $j=1,2.$  \n\n- For ${v}_{1}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =1\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-2)=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {h}_{2} & =1\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 3=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{1}\\in {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{2}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =1\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)=-6\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{2}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$ We do not need to test ${v}_{2}\\cdot {h}_{2}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{3}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-6)\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot (-2)=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{3}\\cdot {h}_{2} & =3\\cdot 3+(-6)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 3=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{3}\\in {H}^{⊥}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80581/selection/74f923e30bd1e60077b4941616bdd8e16717425c5c2d54b9fa80a277550d9802" :answer/id #uuid "1d953562-9b7e-5b35-a92b-af95d99ebf48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80581/selection/9ee5b7299b5081feb73880ff427f94a4f20a0524e7e9f02d2426693a6da8815a" :answer/id #uuid "3637d8af-da86-54c5-a0ea-0c409a667d4e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80581/selection/c775d251c2737ff86ab12a951f39bac6f44f996847b75a21c2b9f77d1a77f1b5" :answer/id #uuid "483a8d0e-b91f-57af-9c93-caa2ce6a7a1b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80581/selection/8bbb9b9c275947ae743c4d231ad6dc61095cead5dcf5e55860f326f0a11358f1" :answer/id #uuid "f717704c-792a-5945-a2e0-bad27270fd5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{3}$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80581/selection/0ee2c133953f3d6ea97ca3917c43b8d8fab218ff0379a1feaf1fee002f694b05" :answer/id #uuid "73495f42-005e-59ec-8c24-18ab2fd69134" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80581/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1fa6ff6-7b02-50a2-be10-2383b8018503" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80581/selection/0ee2c133953f3d6ea97ca3917c43b8d8fab218ff0379a1feaf1fee002f694b05" :answer-field/choices ["q-80581/selection/74f923e30bd1e60077b4941616bdd8e16717425c5c2d54b9fa80a277550d9802" "q-80581/selection/9ee5b7299b5081feb73880ff427f94a4f20a0524e7e9f02d2426693a6da8815a" "q-80581/selection/c775d251c2737ff86ab12a951f39bac6f44f996847b75a21c2b9f77d1a77f1b5" "q-80581/selection/8bbb9b9c275947ae743c4d231ad6dc61095cead5dcf5e55860f326f0a11358f1" "q-80581/selection/0ee2c133953f3d6ea97ca3917c43b8d8fab218ff0379a1feaf1fee002f694b05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80581" :question/id #uuid "2e741dfd-bd80-514a-860d-823db3cd516a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80581" :question/problem "Consider the vector subspace $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}.$ Which of the following vectors belong to ${H}^{⊥}?$\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let  $h=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ A vector  $v$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $v$ is orthogonal to $h.$ So, we have to find the products ${v}_{i}\\cdot h$ for $i=1,2,3.$   \n\n- For ${v}_{1}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot h & =4\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, ${v}_{1}\\in {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{2}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2}\\cdot h & =2\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot (-4)=30\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, ${v}_{2}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{3}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3}\\cdot h & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)=-19\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{3}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${v}_{1}$  only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80581/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb11d128-ee1b-5c35-aefb-1455570d20c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80576/selection/c775d251c2737ff86ab12a951f39bac6f44f996847b75a21c2b9f77d1a77f1b5" :answer/id #uuid "e73f0e06-a224-5143-bcbf-ab5d12ecd20d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80576/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" :answer/id #uuid "0f7568f9-ca77-50be-bccb-1ddc0145f3a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80576/selection/ae1ff8dad45e2c5cacb282945bb7f05d8899845640df9f6d8c53708f78d95913" :answer/id #uuid "d66ae6b7-cace-581f-a405-92eaa867ce59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80576/selection/9ee5b7299b5081feb73880ff427f94a4f20a0524e7e9f02d2426693a6da8815a" :answer/id #uuid "4ac30d9f-65c4-54cd-b89b-1162d23a396f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80576/selection/e59b1317e710cc3efb03339d0dda62b111e50354d142ee4531e7a4057ac1ae98" :answer/id #uuid "ae50014b-6d06-5aaa-9d3c-1928e1eb3e8c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80576/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d3ba89b-f40c-5e5b-98d3-0fd087424214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80576/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" :answer-field/choices ["q-80576/selection/c775d251c2737ff86ab12a951f39bac6f44f996847b75a21c2b9f77d1a77f1b5" "q-80576/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" "q-80576/selection/ae1ff8dad45e2c5cacb282945bb7f05d8899845640df9f6d8c53708f78d95913" "q-80576/selection/9ee5b7299b5081feb73880ff427f94a4f20a0524e7e9f02d2426693a6da8815a" "q-80576/selection/e59b1317e710cc3efb03339d0dda62b111e50354d142ee4531e7a4057ac1ae98"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80576" :question/id #uuid "2706fd95-4749-5416-af7f-b2e6a7351f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80576" :question/problem "Consider the vector subspace $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}.$ Which of the following vectors belong to ${H}^{⊥}?$\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let  $h=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ A vector $v$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $v$ is orthogonal to $h.$ So, we have to find the products ${v}_{i}\\cdot h$ for $i=1,2,3.$  \n\n- For ${v}_{1}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot h & =1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 3=10\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{1}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{2}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2}\\cdot h & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 3=-4\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{2}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{3}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3}\\cdot h & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 3=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{3}\\in {H}^{⊥}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${v}_{3}$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80576/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb11d128-ee1b-5c35-aefb-1455570d20c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80584/selection/74f923e30bd1e60077b4941616bdd8e16717425c5c2d54b9fa80a277550d9802" :answer/id #uuid "7c27e091-9c1a-52ad-837d-3f88b9fcedca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80584/selection/c775d251c2737ff86ab12a951f39bac6f44f996847b75a21c2b9f77d1a77f1b5" :answer/id #uuid "5e0731da-2baa-5423-8272-fa09ec0c509b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80584/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" :answer/id #uuid "4877dd42-1cb2-5b26-8a82-c79864c32c8a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80584/selection/e59b1317e710cc3efb03339d0dda62b111e50354d142ee4531e7a4057ac1ae98" :answer/id #uuid "095b7500-f88e-5c6a-81a6-1f744df796ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{2}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80584/selection/ae1ff8dad45e2c5cacb282945bb7f05d8899845640df9f6d8c53708f78d95913" :answer/id #uuid "eb4261c9-14bb-57ad-a051-e2f96f105354" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80584/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "152aaa61-f97a-50f9-a7ff-79d595302c48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80584/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" :answer-field/choices ["q-80584/selection/74f923e30bd1e60077b4941616bdd8e16717425c5c2d54b9fa80a277550d9802" "q-80584/selection/c775d251c2737ff86ab12a951f39bac6f44f996847b75a21c2b9f77d1a77f1b5" "q-80584/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" "q-80584/selection/e59b1317e710cc3efb03339d0dda62b111e50354d142ee4531e7a4057ac1ae98" "q-80584/selection/ae1ff8dad45e2c5cacb282945bb7f05d8899845640df9f6d8c53708f78d95913"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80584" :question/id #uuid "63cd77a9-8a5f-5279-a45d-65255e657187" :question/math-academy-id "q-80584" :question/problem "Consider the vector subspace $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}.$ Which of the following vectors belong to ${H}^{⊥}?$ \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}$ and ${h}_{2}.$  \n\nNow, a vector $v$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $v$ is orthogonal to the set of vectors that spans the subspace $H.$ So, we have to find the products ${v}_{i}\\cdot {h}_{j}$ for $i=1,2,3$ and  $j=1,2.$ \n\n- For ${v}_{1}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =3\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 4=19\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, ${v}_{1}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$ We do not need to test ${v}_{1}\\cdot {h}_{2}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{2}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =3\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 4=8\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{2}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$ We do not need to test ${v}_{2}\\cdot {h}_{2}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{3}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =7\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 4=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{3}\\cdot {h}_{2} & =7\\cdot 2+5\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{3}\\in {H}^{⊥}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${v}_{3}$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80584/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb11d128-ee1b-5c35-aefb-1455570d20c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140468/selection/74f923e30bd1e60077b4941616bdd8e16717425c5c2d54b9fa80a277550d9802" :answer/id #uuid "e5374f5c-abd5-55b9-be3f-308ab596bf8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140468/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" :answer/id #uuid "1eb256e3-5266-515b-8c23-0b55d959f13c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140468/selection/9ee5b7299b5081feb73880ff427f94a4f20a0524e7e9f02d2426693a6da8815a" :answer/id #uuid "6967de3e-fda0-5e12-80fa-6328217d2af9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140468/selection/ae1ff8dad45e2c5cacb282945bb7f05d8899845640df9f6d8c53708f78d95913" :answer/id #uuid "8ae7405b-f923-5d5f-8c5c-b51f31ee7fc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140468/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "bb8b970b-3155-52fc-8275-44c8a13f54e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140468/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6bbc6f-3090-583b-a850-44b490470a49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140468/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" :answer-field/choices ["q-140468/selection/74f923e30bd1e60077b4941616bdd8e16717425c5c2d54b9fa80a277550d9802" "q-140468/selection/3b5c09299df187455e033e1efb084c2785900b543e47830f83626bf457d3bce4" "q-140468/selection/9ee5b7299b5081feb73880ff427f94a4f20a0524e7e9f02d2426693a6da8815a" "q-140468/selection/ae1ff8dad45e2c5cacb282945bb7f05d8899845640df9f6d8c53708f78d95913" "q-140468/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140468" :question/id #uuid "2eb17a02-3ec7-5adc-ace9-ee9207acfe63" :question/math-academy-id "q-140468" :question/problem "Consider the vector subspace $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]}.$ Which of the following vectors belong to ${H}^{⊥}?$\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}$ and ${h}_{2}.$ \n\nNow, a vector $v$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $v$ is orthogonal to the set of vectors that spans the subspace $H.$ So, we have to find the products ${v}_{i}\\cdot {h}_{j}$ for $i=1,2,3$ and  $j=1,2.$  \n\n- For ${v}_{1}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =5\\cdot (-6)+(-2)\\cdot 0+6\\cdot 5=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {h}_{2} & =5\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 4+6\\cdot (-11)=-64\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{1}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{2}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =5\\cdot (-6)+(-14)\\cdot 0+(-6)\\cdot 5=-60\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{2}\\notin {H}^{⊥}.$ We do not need to test ${v}_{2}\\cdot {h}_{2}.$\n\n- For ${v}_{3}$, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3}\\cdot {h}_{1} & =5\\cdot (-6)+14\\cdot 0+6\\cdot 5=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{3}\\cdot {h}_{2} & =5\\cdot 2+14\\cdot 4+6\\cdot (-11)=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${v}_{3}\\in {H}^{⊥}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${v}_{3}$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb11d128-ee1b-5c35-aefb-1455570d20c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39625/selection/5a225bcdc8f92f51f7db25d8f4476bf18b66ed3f9a4a70389bc3897cdca25f27" :answer/id #uuid "e8c84d62-9012-5a2a-90f8-309d5fa0fa3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39625/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" :answer/id #uuid "ced44c5f-6c71-5bfa-bfe8-83798798d8a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39625/selection/528912b4c5f94b4c434e0d845715d8bd2c24d5b6f12bb5bc1d6bb75f7b697226" :answer/id #uuid "019fea90-0b41-5eae-9565-d16e1004ef30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39625/selection/c53637fd05f63b37aebf9b4643cfa6c9eceb7cda247a4ad36cabc0dd480e2dc0" :answer/id #uuid "97cc8452-36c3-5c5d-8a31-9c0abb869fad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39625/selection/7ada71e519e5431207e571991cbc3ecfa003ed6a18f9bd6eb82e86268a24fc19" :answer/id #uuid "ee94cb2c-2e03-5847-a83c-60b3f2cee888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39625/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98004a82-5a17-50b1-8ac6-40115640f425" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39625/selection/c53637fd05f63b37aebf9b4643cfa6c9eceb7cda247a4ad36cabc0dd480e2dc0" :answer-field/choices ["q-39625/selection/5a225bcdc8f92f51f7db25d8f4476bf18b66ed3f9a4a70389bc3897cdca25f27" "q-39625/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" "q-39625/selection/528912b4c5f94b4c434e0d845715d8bd2c24d5b6f12bb5bc1d6bb75f7b697226" "q-39625/selection/c53637fd05f63b37aebf9b4643cfa6c9eceb7cda247a4ad36cabc0dd480e2dc0" "q-39625/selection/7ada71e519e5431207e571991cbc3ecfa003ed6a18f9bd6eb82e86268a24fc19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39625" :question/id #uuid "d5aabf0b-4546-5bc0-a1a8-38812d835d5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39625" :question/problem "Find ${H}^{⊥}$, if $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}$ and ${h}_{2}.$ \n\nA vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0$ and $x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0 \\\\ x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one), so ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our orthogonal complement is\n\n$$\n{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39625/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2f7e06-54f8-5a9b-a926-362fb087b59c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39625"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/selection/6dd2cfa7d7cbcbcc84bd5effc5fab4c9b8c1682b3bb21c80f7136001e3036c90" :answer/id #uuid "a5f97b58-7bd4-5736-b682-c2906b5dc9b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/selection/15aa5158a63ae21ae09e9dece186da3669d10ceb90ec12310dde180f2a81dc1d" :answer/id #uuid "a55111ab-339f-58c4-9f17-45bf9ef7ca5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/selection/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" :answer/id #uuid "4aae0962-46b5-5b00-8c68-ae1860310fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/selection/f64e376bfaa4d22b6756953610ba2f9d92564306c58ad1273f1969e8f73754ed" :answer/id #uuid "8cac39d6-5775-55a1-b9a6-27e278a0d412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/selection/abc22af8800e8889dc7c5b92858ee2d1c27d174c12815983f27101758b8c4dce" :answer/id #uuid "18f0a33b-8a03-5992-9fcf-75ecfee9ccbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f82fa42-5949-59e4-909a-c58936705442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39626/selection/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" :answer-field/choices ["q-39626/selection/6dd2cfa7d7cbcbcc84bd5effc5fab4c9b8c1682b3bb21c80f7136001e3036c90" "q-39626/selection/15aa5158a63ae21ae09e9dece186da3669d10ceb90ec12310dde180f2a81dc1d" "q-39626/selection/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" "q-39626/selection/f64e376bfaa4d22b6756953610ba2f9d92564306c58ad1273f1969e8f73754ed" "q-39626/selection/abc22af8800e8889dc7c5b92858ee2d1c27d174c12815983f27101758b8c4dce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39626" :question/id #uuid "43c590fa-d89b-58cd-94e7-3ff278816239" :question/math-academy-id "q-39626" :question/problem "Find a basis of ${H}^{⊥}$ if  $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0$ and $x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0 \\\\ x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd one), so ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the  second equation we get ${x}_{2}=0$ and then from the first equation we obtain  ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}.$ So, any vector in ${H}^{⊥}$ has the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of ${H}^{⊥}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39626/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2f7e06-54f8-5a9b-a926-362fb087b59c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39626"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39916/selection/446b8f8a31c9553d532c87a0e768367bd514dda196ccd0a48091c05ea1d06d3e" :answer/id #uuid "4060b23f-b621-566f-aedb-bbf5c214f225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39916/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" :answer/id #uuid "d8d56431-6bc6-5392-8f22-95bef4f62458" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39916/selection/b6b778addf670f099d2233fd13653cb5d5683d318a500fa1c4f21d7e608b0a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9ac1ee39-fcdc-5877-ab99-2a27ca4e7fd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39916/selection/772bc22f7b758c47b624ab6d3ad565fc79c83be64664ae796d8ea08b9b02d680" :answer/id #uuid "37262b32-3266-5efd-b22c-3e782f553a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39916/selection/154423c02ec9307662b4c241809977f1b966c805a9bdb686a0e40677d89ce8cb" :answer/id #uuid "343d271b-13d8-5e6a-b813-b7759f7c6979" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39916/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a850056-2423-5e1c-a70e-e59f359677f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39916/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" :answer-field/choices ["q-39916/selection/446b8f8a31c9553d532c87a0e768367bd514dda196ccd0a48091c05ea1d06d3e" "q-39916/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" "q-39916/selection/b6b778addf670f099d2233fd13653cb5d5683d318a500fa1c4f21d7e608b0a3b" "q-39916/selection/772bc22f7b758c47b624ab6d3ad565fc79c83be64664ae796d8ea08b9b02d680" "q-39916/selection/154423c02ec9307662b4c241809977f1b966c805a9bdb686a0e40677d89ce8cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39916" :question/id #uuid "5bafd46f-4d0d-5847-af92-1b47a9fb2b93" :question/math-academy-id "q-39916" :question/problem "Find ${H}^{⊥}$, if $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}$ and ${h}_{2}.$ \n\nA vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0$ and $x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {x}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-9{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=0$  and from the first one, we obtain ${x}_{1}=0.$ So, the solution to the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, our orthogonal complement is\n\n$$\n{H}^{⊥}={0}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39916/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2f7e06-54f8-5a9b-a926-362fb087b59c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39916"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39633/selection/39ffa0ec5785b36eebaa7724638842edac5b58d5cf65a60efa30dcb9eb98b185" :answer/id #uuid "a8d7394f-767f-551a-8c8b-7c67a3e2200a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39633/selection/dcdb7288e6e1477c7d786c773cea7e884f0ed538f226be65069ad79364e68760" :answer/id #uuid "3a8541b3-a914-5227-9fc1-234d1ac8ba0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39633/selection/4f3fac65f1383961493e543b439d03f4fcb9ea8d6420f2180bd6234e7ba83bb1" :answer/id #uuid "76a9f39b-0de5-59a8-b567-aa1c62d49d37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39633/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" :answer/id #uuid "808ddb04-a02f-5704-985c-45666cd27ca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39633/selection/679cb6c232fc1b89e6440ec4bdcafc298a5ce0c92c9ca68ff054846d99a59e5e" :answer/id #uuid "3f1ad34d-f427-5d79-b170-5854331b0b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{H}^{⊥}={[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39633/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "328371b9-0dee-5c7b-9f07-147871d90280" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39633/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" :answer-field/choices ["q-39633/selection/39ffa0ec5785b36eebaa7724638842edac5b58d5cf65a60efa30dcb9eb98b185" "q-39633/selection/dcdb7288e6e1477c7d786c773cea7e884f0ed538f226be65069ad79364e68760" "q-39633/selection/4f3fac65f1383961493e543b439d03f4fcb9ea8d6420f2180bd6234e7ba83bb1" "q-39633/selection/0b9282592ccaa1cff42241dafee8ad6072b192f09540dc7311137854ca26123e" "q-39633/selection/679cb6c232fc1b89e6440ec4bdcafc298a5ce0c92c9ca68ff054846d99a59e5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39633" :question/id #uuid "7e102f80-1de4-5da6-83a4-86ff00dee1d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-39633" :question/problem "Find  ${H}^{⊥}$, if $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}$ and ${h}_{2}.$ \n\nA vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0$ and $x\\cdot {h}_{2}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1}=0 \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which we reduce to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=0$  and from the first one, we obtain ${x}_{1}=0.$ So, the solution to the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, our orthogonal complement is\n\n$$\n{H}^{⊥}={0}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39633/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2f7e06-54f8-5a9b-a926-362fb087b59c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39633"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134172 :